9. Conclusions
In this work we have presented a mathematical contribution to explain the numerical instabilities encountered using time-partitioned schemes in presence of certain combinations of physical and geometrical parameters in the simulation of a class of fluid–structure interaction problems. Our target application is
4526 P. Causin et al. / Comput. Methods Appl. Mech. Engrg. 194 (2005) 4506–4527


the simulation of blood flow in large human arteries, but the discussion applies as well to FSI problems encountered in other applications in which an incompressible fluid interacts with a thin elastic structure. These kind of numerical instabilities seem to arise specifically in the context of incompressible fluid models. Thus, this aspect plays a crucial role in devising stable and efficient coupling schemes for these class of problems and it deserves future investigation.
